                  "type": "heading",
                  "level": 2,
                  "text": "ASME SB-446"
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "level": 4,
                  "text": "ASME SB-446"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The ASME SB-446 specification covers nickel-chromium-molybdenum- columbium (UNS N06625), nickel-chromium-molybdenum-silicon alloy (UNS N0621 9), and Nickel- Chromium-Molybdenum-Tungsten Alloy (UNS N06650) in the form of hot-worked rod and bar and cold-worked rod in the conditions shown in Table 2."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "UNS N06625 (Nickel Alloy 625) products are furnished in two grades of different heat-treated conditions:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Grade 1 (Annealed)—Material is normally employed in service temperatures up to 1100°F (593°C)."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Grade 2 (Solution Annealed)—Material is normally employed in service temperatures above 1100°F (593°C) when resistance to creep and rupture is required."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Alloys UNS N06219 and UNS N06650 are supplied in solution annealed condition only."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
